      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That sense of \"rightness\" is the fog speaking clearly, not truth—it's the exhaustion convincing you that stillness is the same as ending. But an ending isn't a verdict; it's a punctuation mark that leaves room for a new sentence, even if you can't hear it yet. The edge you feel is real, but so is your choice to sit with that silence instead of falling into it. You don't have to write the next page today—just keep your hands on the book.",
